    "anchor_unavailable", "malformed", "unknown_signer", "superseded_signer", "wrong_authority",
    "binding_mismatch", "revision_regressed", "revision_conflict", "unknown_target",
)

NOTE = {
    "corpus": (
        "The cases named m_<path>_<candidate>_<approver> are the enrolment matrix: every combination of "
        "authoriser path (lan, an authorization object; phone, an ORI-ENROL-V1 text), candidate kind (lan, sms) "
        "and candidate approver (minted, own, other). The cases named e_<path>_<condition> are the authoriser "
        "eligibility block: every combination of authoriser path (lan, phone) and authoriser condition (absent, "
        "not_active, wrong_kind, not_preexisting, eligible). The cases named x_<table>_<row>_<axes> are the "
        "refusal sweep, each decided by its row: steps (the Order-of-refusal steps) over every registry "
        "operation, and over evidence_commission for payload_too_large and invalid_arguments; cp (Challenges "
        "presented) over recover, and over local_seed (a lan challenge) and enrol (a lan or sms challenge) each "
        "x presented candidate kind (lan, sms, whatsapp), a presented kind other than the challenge's being "
        "decided at candidate_changed unless an earlier row fires; challenge_unavailable over the presented "
        "candidate kind alone, no challenge being held, and site_binding_mismatch also with no challenge held, "
        "over recover and the presented kind for local_seed and enrol; an "
        "expired sms challenge sitting between "
        "the 60-second challenge window and the 10-minute possession window; ch "
        "(Challenge) for an enrolment over candidate kind (lan, sms) x request approver (null, named), except "
        "phone_pending_for_value (sms only), channel_unauthenticated (whatsapp, and sms while the runtime has "
        "no authenticated SMS ingress) and approver_revoked and "
        "approver_unknown (named only); rc, ls, rv and bd (Recover, Local seed, Revoke, Binding) alone; en "
        "(Enrol) over authoriser path (lan, phone) x candidate kind (lan, sms), and from challenge_stale on, "
        "where the registry is held, also x candidate approver (minted, own, and other up to "
        "authorizer_not_approver; registry_unavailable has no approver axis), except that "
        "signature_invalid_authorization is lan-path only, possession_invalid and signature_invalid_possession "
        "are lan-candidate only, "
        "phone_pending_for_value is sms-candidate only, authorizer_not_approver is other only and "
        "approver_revoked minted only; ms (member strictness) over member form (escaped_duplicate, "
        "case_variant, unknown_member) x location (top, candidate, authorization, possession, document), "
        "malformed inside a document and invalid_arguments elsewhere. "
        "Each case is one request on the operator socket and the runtime's answer to it under the context "
        "given. Every case is independent; contexts do not carry over. A replay sends `request` as its UTF-8 "
        "bytes followed by one LF, from a peer with the context's credentials, and compares the answer with "
        "`expected`."
    ),
    "request": (
        "The exact bytes the client sends, as UTF-8 text; `request_bytes` is their length in UTF-8 bytes. The "
        "runtime reads the bytes before the first LF, so a request that holds an LF is judged on the bytes "
        "before it and the bound is compared with their length."
    ),
    "terminated": (
        "true: the client sends one LF after `request`. false: the connection ends after `request` with no "
        "further byte, so a request that holds no LF ends before any LF."
    ),
    "signatures": (
        "A signed object is a possession (verified under the candidate's value at Local seed's or Enrol's "
        "possession signature_invalid row), an authorization (under the named active credential's value, at "
        "Enrol's first signature_invalid row) or a revocation document (under its signing_key, at Revoke's "
        "signature_invalid row). A case may carry a signed object whose signature does not verify only when "
        "its answer is decided by a step of Order of refusal, by a row of Challenges presented, or by a row "
        "of the operation's table that comes before that object's signature row or is that row. In every "
        "other case each signed object the request carries verifies under its key."
    ),
    "expected.changes": (
        "Every state change the answer commits, sorted, from this closed vocabulary: "
        "challenge_added:<challenge_id> (a pending challenge with its deadline); code_sent:<challenge_id> (a "
        "possession code sent to the challenge's phone candidate); used:<challenge_id> (the challenge marked "
        "used); registry_created:<identity_epoch> (an empty initialized registry under that epoch and the "
        "verified site: revision 1, last external revision 0, credential sequence 0, no credentials or "
        "tombstones); challenges_cleared, phone_authorizations_cleared and pending_phone_cleared (every held "
        "challenge, received phone authorization and pending phone operation removed); "
        "credential_added:<credential_id> (the candidate made active); sequence:<n> and revision:<n> (the new "
        "credential sequence and registry revision); pending_phone_added:<value> (a pending phone operation "
        "for the candidate); credential_tombstoned:<credential_id> and value_tombstoned:<value> (an active "
        "credential removed, its ID and value tombstoned); approver_tombstoned:<approver_id>; and "
        "last_external_revision:<n>. A refusal lists [] or, when it consumes its challenge, only "
        "used:<challenge_id>. Every successful recover lists challenges_cleared, phone_authorizations_cleared "
        "and pending_phone_cleared, whether or not anything was held, and still lists used:<challenge_id> for "
        "the challenge it consumes and clears in the same transaction. registry_created implies revision 1, "
        "last external revision 0 and credential sequence 0, which are not listed separately. The recorded "
        "fingerprint of the last applied revocation document changes with last_external_revision and has no "
        "token of its own."
    ),
    "context.keys_failing_admission": (
        "The configured anchors' keys and active lan_ed25519 credential keys (canonical Base64 of the raw "
        "32 bytes) that this fixture deliberately holds although they fail ed25519-key-admission/v1. Every "
        "other key in the context passes it."
    ),
    "context.device_id": "The running runtime's device identity.",
    "context.verified_site_id": "The device.site_id of the runtime's verified provisioning configuration.",
    "context.peer_uid": (
        "The peer's effective user ID from kernel peer credentials; null when they cannot be established."
    ),
    "context.operator_uid": "The installed operator identity; null when none is installed.",
    "context.registry_operation_in_flight": "Whether another admitted registry operation is in flight.",
    "context.anchor_available": "Whether the current provisioning anchor is present and usable.",
    "context.anchors": (
        "The configured anchors' raw Ed25519 public keys, canonical Base64: the current provisioning "
        "anchor, the previous provisioning anchor, and one anchor of another class."
    ),
    "context.registry": (
        "null when the registry is locked. Otherwise its site binding, identity epoch, registry revision, "
        "last external revision, the SHA-256 (lowercase hex) of the Profile 2 canonical JSON of the last "
        "applied revocation document or null, credential sequence, active credentials (each with its "
        "approver ID, credential ID, channel, value as in a challenge candidate, and enrolment sequence), "
        "the credentials tombstoned in this epoch (each with its credential ID and the approver ID it belonged "
        "to), the approver IDs tombstoned in this epoch, and the values tombstoned in this epoch: revoking a "
        "credential tombstones its value as well as its ID."
    ),
    "context.challenges": (
        "Challenges the runtime holds, each with its challenge object, its state (pending; used, already "
        "presented; or expired, its deadline passed and not yet presented), the registry's credential "
        "sequence when it was created, and elapsed_ms, the monotonic milliseconds since it was created. A "
        "challenge not used is expired exactly when elapsed_ms exceeds 60,000, the challenge window, whatever "
        "its candidate's channel; the separate 10-minute phone possession window never extends it. A "
        "challenge absent from the list is one the runtime does not hold."
    ),
    "context.phone_authorizations": (
        "ORI-ENROL-V1 texts the runtime has received and attributed through a phone channel's authenticated "
        "ingress, in the order they arrived: the challenge ID and challenge SHA-256 the text carries, and the "
        "credential ID of the sender. The first entry for a challenge ID is that challenge's authorization, "
        "whoever its sender; a later entry for the same challenge ID is ignored. A sender the runtime could not "
        "attribute to a credential is represented by a credential ID that is neither active nor tombstoned."
    ),
    "context.pending_phone_values": "Phone values with a pending phone operation, on either phone channel.",
    "context.authenticated_phone_channels": (
        "The phone channels that have an authenticated ingress at the runtime. In v1 only sms can; an empty list "
        "means the runtime has no authenticated SMS ingress, so an sms candidate is channel_unauthenticated. The "
        "set is fixed for a run, so a held challenge whose candidate is on a phone channel the list leaves out "
        "is not a valid context."
    ),
    "context.minted": (
        "The values the runtime's CSPRNG yields for the next challenge: challenge ID, approver ID, "
        "credential ID, and the prospective identity epoch for a recover challenge. null unless the request "
        "is a well-formed challenge request that reaches the Challenge table."
    ),
    "expected": (
        "ok true with the exact `result` object, or ok false with the `error.code`. `consumes_challenge` "
        "appears for the operations that present a challenge: whether the named challenge is used "
        "afterwards because of this request. A refusal changes nothing else."
    ),
    "keys": (
        "Ed25519 private keys are SHA-256 of 'ori operator-socket/v3 <label> test key'; challenge_sha256 is "
        "SHA-256 of the challenge's Profile 2 canonical JSON. Test keys only."
    ),
}


